{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "The one catalog of the app's groups and tools (F20, M12). A tool is one thing a person can do; a group is a set of related tools with one switch. The shell (app/src-tauri/src/groups.rs, include_str!), the engine (runner/src/groups.ts) and the pages (app/src/groups.ts) all read this file, so a tool belongs to exactly one group, everywhere. Every hotkey (keymap.rs), every shell command (main.rs generate_handler), every command the engine takes (protocol/index.ts COMMANDS) and every mode of agent.start is listed in exactly one tool; tests in all three places fail when one is missing or listed twice. The group core has no switch: Stop everything, the safety rules, the key, the daily limit, Delete everything and house rules can never be switched off. A tool may also have its own switch (a settings key, `switch`): it is on only while its group is on and its own switch is not off, and a tool that is off is held back exactly like a group that is off (its keys let go, its commands refused, its buttons not drawn, its permissions never asked). F28: Second Look also follows secondLook.on, Type by voice talk.dictate and Draw it drawIt.on. The prompt group (prompt.on) was split out of voice (the overhaul spec, 3.4): voice.on is talking only, prompt.on the keys that read text you select (Prompt help, the error explainer, Second Look). Only ids live here; every name and sentence a person reads is in app/src/strings.ts (rule 21).",
  "offLine": "That is switched off in Settings. Turn it back on there to use it.",
